  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q6-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Ahmed walks into a shop and buys 1 kg of apples, 2 kg of bananas and 3 kg of carrots, spending $\\$16$. Ben walks into the same shop and buys 3 kg of apples, 2 kg of bananas and 1 kg carrots, spending $\\$20$. Connor walks into the same shop and buys 1 kg of apples, 1 kg of bananas and 1 kg of carrots. How much does she spend? Note: there is not enough information here to determine the individual prices.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$9$.\n\nAdd the two purchase equations and divide by 4.",
      "worked": "Let $a$, $b$ and $c$ be the prices per kilogram of apples, bananas and carrots, respectively, in dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a+2b+3c&=16\\qquad\\text{(1)}\\\\3a+2b+c&=20\\qquad\\text{(2)}\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdding (1) and (2):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4a+4b+4c&=36\\\\a+b+c&=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nConnor spends $\\$9$. The total can be found without determining the individual prices.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
